    "body": "## Problem and resulting behavior\n\nA nonzero interpolation row can be a pure x-polynomial that pads its zeros with cancelling point pairs. This update adds a tight norm acceptance certificate using the actual cubic f=X^3+aX+b and N=u^2-f*v^2. For a nonzero pair, distinct selected curve x's and degree N<=support size, the source proves exact simple norm roots, nonzero selected v denominators and the exact signed affine zero locus. [pcc:unverified]\n\nThe new direction targets a tight colored interpolation row. Pure nodal padding is excluded for nonempty support; duplicate-coordinate and empty-constant controls remain explicit. The earlier exact-kernel injectivity witness applies when t<=dU, whereas positive tight caps imply dU<t; projection to v is injective within each selected kernel in that range. No equivalent useful-regime search lower bound is inferred. [pcc:unverified]\n\nA proposed shortcut through the fixed cubic quotient was tested symbolically and rejected as a complete selector: a bare norm congruence can pass while its required polynomial square quotient does not exist. The actual square-quotient and selected-sign conditions remain. [pcc:unverified]\n\n## Validation and limits\n\n- Twenty-four maintained generic laws and five symbolic applications compile. Actual colored signed-locus, opposite-sign, duplicate-node, empty-support and useful-cap projection applications pass. Twenty-four named axiom prints use standard dependencies only. [pcc:unverified]\n- Final local all-tracked canonical gate001:597/0/0, delta31 from566 is24 owner laws+5 applications+2 defining equations; no removals. Raw infrastructure/proof-interface failures are retained; no proof-limit/trust/inventory/linter exception, custom axiom or native_decide. [pcc:unverified]\n- All406 hashes match, including378 older pins;22 ledger rows retain published f30821-row/main0179-row exact byte/parsed prefixes. Scoped statement `PCC-20261116-bda7ce` remains unverified; no independently signed verdict or identity certificate. [pcc:unverified]\n\nPrincipal-divisor/pole identification and the actual elliptic point-sum bridge remain HAND. Fast colored nonzero extraction, original-input useful yield and complete classical subexponential prime-field ECDLP remain unmet. A further monic norm normalization is written next-step analysis, not a newly compiled endpoint or measured speedup. [pcc:unverified]\n\nNo new scientific/numerical/field/curve/Sage/LLL/native qualification, paid job, image build/pull or control execution. The older first-endpoint control remains UNEXECUTED,1PythonAST/1JSONparse only. Live cost and actual runtime/caller/capacity/custody admission remain missing;2USD proposal is not a grant or known balance. [pcc:unverified]\n\nLatest report: docs/norm-saturated-interpolation-20261116.md. Frozen source/plan/report/PDF/control/raw evidence and the unrelated Velu probe are unchanged.\n",
